// "DealsDamageToEach" — the mass-burn / board-wipe damage shape (the
// damage-sweeper family): an object deals damage ([CR#120.1]) to every
// member of a recipient class at once ([CR#608.2d] distributive each —
// iterating a many-`Binder` binds each selected object in turn as the
// anaphor `It`). The migrations parser's `parse_deal_damage`/
// `damage_target` production reads the recipient-class phrase (via the
// shared object-target filter grammar) and emits this invocation with that
// filter as the second argument, since the generic macro-template
// fallthrough can't itself synthesize an arbitrary `Predicate` from
// English.
//
// Actual users: the generated `plugins/wizards` corpus invokes this macro
// 162 times (that migrations pipeline's own "deals N damage to each
// <class>" shape); in hand-authored `plugins/canon`, the sole user is
// Chandra, Torch of Defiance's [+1] impulse `if_not` branch ("~ deals 2
// damage to each opponent"). Canon's own `Pyroclasm.ron`/`Flame Rift.ron`
// (previously cited here as users) author the identical shape directly as a
// raw `Each(binder: Existing(SelectAll(...)), effect: DealDamage(...))`
// instead of through this macro, so they are not actually users of it;
// "Hour of Devastation" (also previously cited here) has no card file in
// this corpus at all (only a `.ron.todo` stub under `plugins/wizards`).
//
// `source` is fixed at `This` — every corpus usage is a spell/ability
// naming its own source ("~ deals …"), never a foreign dealer; a card that
// needs a different source is a distinct (unbuilt) shape.
//
// Usage: DealsDamageToEach(2, Creature) / DealsDamageToEach(1,
// OpponentOf(Ref(You))) / DealsDamageToEach(3, And([Creature,
// ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You)))])).
(
    name: "DealsDamageToEach",
    template: "~ deals ${0} damage to each ${1}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Count, Predicate],
    frames: ["~ deals <Param(0)> damage to each <Param(1)>"],
    body: Each(binder: Existing(SelectAll(Param(1))), effect: DealDamage(This, Param(0), It)),
)
